      "mergedPostDetails": "Unsure why exactly this happens. Test avatar is Ukon Second Type: both avatars are identical in Unity, save for the one avatar descriptor additionally being set up for facetracking.\n\nThe one with facetracking sinks into the ground about hip-height, similar to bicycle pose, but still animated/tracked correctly. Using an emote/Action Layer snaps to the expected position for its duration. When Selfie Expression is not tracking, the avatar goes cross-eyed (unsure if related).\n\nTested in both Desktop and VR with others saying I am in the ground each time.\n\nNon-FT visemes + eyelook: avtr_9c769218-351c-434a-88f5-1025e1e8a028\n\nNative Face Tracking: avtr_df9728b8-31c1-43c3-9613-9e5d9baf484c",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[SDK 3.10.6-beta.4] Remote avatar sinks into ground when native face tracking is set up",
